1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,597
Stand up tall, reach out your hand.

2
00:00:03,680 --> 00:00:06,797
Cut through the wind and make a stand!

3
00:00:06,880 --> 00:00:11,240
The paint within brings
out a map of your own.

4
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:19,597
To the left and the right,
all we saw stormy nights.

5
00:00:19,680 --> 00:00:22,877
All the rough winds and
waves coming day after day?

6
00:00:22,960 --> 00:00:28,777
And the values we had were about to
collapse Oh, just where do we go next?

7
00:00:28,860 --> 00:00:35,440
And as we look down to the compass in
hand Is it showing us the right direction?

8
00:00:35,740 --> 00:00:38,637
All we know is nobody
here knows it for certain.

9
00:00:38,720 --> 00:00:41,957
So close your eyes and breathe in deeply.

10
00:00:42,040 --> 00:00:45,157
And listen to your soul.

11
00:00:45,240 --> 00:00:48,117
You'll see a path in front of you.

12
00:00:48,200 --> 00:00:51,537
And you'll know just where you need to go.

13
00:00:51,620 --> 00:00:55,817
So stand up tall, reach out your hand.

14
00:00:55,900 --> 00:00:59,037
Cut through the wind and make us stand.

15
00:00:59,120 --> 00:01:02,900
Don't let the darkness
win, just break through.

16
00:01:04,620 --> 00:01:08,137
I'll do it my own way,
that's what's best for me.

17
00:01:08,220 --> 00:01:11,797
And you do it your way,
that's how it's got to be.

18
00:01:11,880 --> 00:01:15,377
We're moving forward, now I'm ready.

19
00:01:15,460 --> 00:01:19,217
But at times it's okay
to get help on the way.

20
00:01:19,300 --> 00:01:21,757
For the future ahead, burning bright.

21
00:01:21,840 --> 00:01:24,197
For what's ahead you see?

22
00:01:24,280 --> 00:01:27,557
Is beyond your wildest dreams.

23
00:01:27,640 --> 00:01:31,797
So stand up tall, reach out your hand,

24
00:01:31,880 --> 00:01:34,997
cut through the wind and make A stand,

25
00:01:35,080 --> 00:01:38,717
don't let the darkness
win, just break through.

26
00:01:38,800 --> 00:01:44,097
We'll do it our way,
the best that we know.

27
00:01:44,180 --> 00:01:47,937
With tears and doubts and tone,
we'll go where we all want to go.

28
00:01:48,020 --> 00:01:52,580
The page within brings colors of our own.

29
00:02:13,400 --> 00:02:16,635
I'll finish you before you
even have a chance to fight.

30
00:02:28,560 --> 00:02:30,100
I don't think so.

31
00:02:30,640 --> 00:02:32,500
Kawamatsu, splendid work.

32
00:02:32,740 --> 00:02:35,357
Let's join the Straw Hats
and take out the big guys.

33
00:02:35,440 --> 00:02:37,417
Don't even think about it, you two.

34
00:02:37,500 --> 00:02:39,400
It isn't our place to help them.

35
00:02:40,200 --> 00:02:41,600
Not in this battle.

36
00:02:42,380 --> 00:02:43,660
Can't you see that?

37
00:02:44,500 --> 00:02:46,260
I don't understand, boss.

38
00:02:46,500 --> 00:02:48,657
They're fighting the lead performers.

39
00:02:48,740 --> 00:02:53,200
We must keep both our enemies and
our allies away from the battle

40
00:02:53,860 --> 00:02:55,660
Look at their faces.

41
00:02:56,120 --> 00:02:58,820
They're saying don't get in our way

42
00:03:12,200 --> 00:03:14,100
On top of the red line

43
00:03:14,860 --> 00:03:17,140
Only thing up there is Marie Joie.

44
00:03:17,360 --> 00:03:18,320
There's no gods.

45
00:03:23,400 --> 00:03:26,740
It's not like you to be
superstitious. What gives?

46
00:03:27,160 --> 00:03:29,220
Are you drunk or something, Pops?

47
00:03:29,500 --> 00:03:30,680
Maybe so.

48
00:03:32,860 --> 00:03:35,517
There's nothing worth
seeing up in Marie Joie.

49
00:03:35,600 --> 00:03:38,129
Just a bunch of stuck-up
celestial dragons.

50
00:03:41,580 --> 00:03:43,177
And they're no gods.

51
00:03:43,260 --> 00:03:45,966
I'm not talking about
the world we know today.

52
00:03:46,320 --> 00:03:50,980
I'm talking about the way things were in
the ancient past, long before Marijoa,

53
00:03:51,420 --> 00:03:53,126
before the Celestial Dragons.

54
00:03:53,700 --> 00:03:58,320
They say there was a land of
gods up there, lost to the ages.

55
00:03:58,980 --> 00:04:00,320
I don't know, Pops.

56
00:04:00,520 --> 00:04:03,932
Whoever told you that was
either crazy or playing a prank.

57
00:04:06,280 --> 00:04:11,760
It sounds like a fairy tale, but
this world is full of strange things.

58
00:04:27,580 --> 00:04:29,037
What's the matter with you?

59
00:04:29,120 --> 00:04:30,537
Can you stop daydreaming?

60
00:04:30,620 --> 00:04:32,208
We're in a fight right now.

61
00:04:33,600 --> 00:04:36,012
Guess I was waiting for you to rescue me.

62
00:04:36,160 --> 00:04:37,300
Stop making jokes.

63
00:04:37,620 --> 00:04:39,208
We need to get out of here.

64
00:04:41,300 --> 00:04:43,120
Izo, do you believe in God?

65
00:04:44,020 --> 00:04:46,057
You sound like Pops when he was drunk.

66
00:04:46,140 --> 00:04:49,157
Yo, wake up, you're rookies!

67
00:04:49,240 --> 00:04:52,828
You boys better check yourselves
before you wreck yourselves.

68
00:04:53,480 --> 00:04:57,500
And by the way, nothing you've
thrown at us has done a damn thing!

69
00:04:59,600 --> 00:05:02,540
Let me remind you what they call us.

70
00:05:05,180 --> 00:05:06,340
The Drought.

71
00:05:10,080 --> 00:05:10,910
Wildfire.

72
00:05:12,940 --> 00:05:14,620
And Plague!

73
00:05:15,960 --> 00:05:19,580
We're the three calamities
that protect Commander Kaido!

74
00:05:19,960 --> 00:05:24,019
We're called the lead performers
because we always take center stage!

75
00:05:37,740 --> 00:05:39,580
Hey, what's up with you?

76
00:05:40,200 --> 00:05:41,757
I don't know how to describe it,

77
00:05:41,840 --> 00:05:45,777
but ever since I took off that stupid
raid suit, my body has felt off.

78
00:05:45,860 --> 00:05:47,507
You better not drag me down.

79
00:05:47,660 --> 00:05:49,657
I didn't say I felt sick, all right?

80
00:05:49,740 --> 00:05:51,211
Just feels kind of weird.

81
00:05:51,680 --> 00:05:53,445
Oh, weird, like your eyebrows?

82
00:05:53,820 --> 00:05:55,900
I said my body, you jackass!

83
00:06:02,880 --> 00:06:04,400
That's one you owe me.

84
00:06:06,620 --> 00:06:07,580
Bridal grabber!

85
00:06:09,580 --> 00:06:10,900
I don't owe you shit!

86
00:06:21,560 --> 00:06:24,680
I heard all of Judge's kids are cyborgs.

87
00:06:24,840 --> 00:06:26,664
What part of you is artificial?

88
00:06:27,500 --> 00:06:30,040
Vinsmoke Judge is as crazy as they come.

89
00:06:30,340 --> 00:06:32,340
Bet he got real creative with you.

90
00:06:32,580 --> 00:06:35,180
So, is that burning
leg of yours a machine?

91
00:06:35,740 --> 00:06:40,160
Hate to break it to you, pal, but
unlike my siblings, I'm 100 % human.

92
00:06:40,400 --> 00:06:43,300
Humans can't light themselves
on fire, you moron.

93
00:06:43,420 --> 00:06:46,180
And I know damn well
you're not a Lunarian.

94
00:06:48,040 --> 00:06:49,100
Watch and learn.

95
00:06:50,280 --> 00:06:51,920
This is all natural.

96
00:06:52,280 --> 00:06:56,692
My passion is hotter than fire, so you
better believe I can bring the heat.

97
00:06:59,220 --> 00:07:01,780
I can cook sea monsters with this leg.

98
00:07:02,040 --> 00:07:03,780
I'll cook a dinosaur, too.

99
00:07:06,940 --> 00:07:11,220
I'm gonna show you cyborg technology
that even Vegapot can't touch!

100
00:07:11,500 --> 00:07:13,340
Hope you enjoy the show!

101
00:07:14,380 --> 00:07:17,120
Hey, pay attention, you big-ass mummy!

102
00:07:32,540 --> 00:07:34,658
What the hell kind of blade is that?

103
00:07:41,140 --> 00:07:44,740
You're not a swordsman
you're a killing machine.

104
00:07:50,400 --> 00:07:54,037
Unlike you I don't need formal
style to cut someone down.

105
00:07:54,120 --> 00:07:58,557
No good point you never called yourself
a swordsman in the first place.

106
00:07:58,640 --> 00:08:02,097
Have it your way who
knows how this will go?

107
00:08:02,180 --> 00:08:06,592
By the end of this fight, I might be
tearing your throat out with my teeth.

108
00:08:09,040 --> 00:08:11,660
I'll do whatever it takes to win.

109
00:08:12,400 --> 00:08:13,640
Is that Enma?

110
00:08:15,040 --> 00:08:16,680
It is indeed, boss.

111
00:08:19,280 --> 00:08:23,517
Although I had my misgivings, when Lady
Hiyori said she would give Enma to him,

112
00:08:23,600 --> 00:08:25,894
there was a reason I couldn't stop her.

113
00:08:29,680 --> 00:08:30,957
That sword he took.

114
00:08:31,040 --> 00:08:33,417
If it truly is Shusui?

115
00:08:33,500 --> 00:08:35,617
You should return it to the land of Wano.

116
00:08:35,700 --> 00:08:36,797
Not a chance.

117
00:08:36,880 --> 00:08:38,600
I told you it's my sword.

118
00:08:40,280 --> 00:08:42,221
Then I'll give you a replacement.

119
00:08:43,220 --> 00:08:44,337
It is a sword.

120
00:08:44,420 --> 00:08:47,257
That was handed down to
me From my late father.

121
00:08:47,340 --> 00:08:49,660
Would that be a fair trade?

122
00:08:55,240 --> 00:08:58,260
As long as you can give
me a replacement, fine.

123
00:09:07,460 --> 00:09:11,620
You know, it's strange because
he's a pirate from a foreign land.

124
00:09:11,860 --> 00:09:16,560
But when I look at him, I can't help
but see the young dime-mule of Ringo.

125
00:09:25,860 --> 00:09:28,720
Shimotuki Ushimaru, fighting with us!

126
00:09:31,400 --> 00:09:32,380
That's true!

127
00:09:32,660 --> 00:09:34,836
Why, even their swordplay is similar!

128
00:09:37,920 --> 00:09:39,360
There's another thing.

129
00:09:39,640 --> 00:09:43,581
Lord Ushimaru descended from the
God of the Blade Shimotsuki Ryuma.

130
00:09:44,240 --> 00:09:49,160
The fact that Zorojuro returned Shusui
to the land of Wano feels like fate.

131
00:10:02,700 --> 00:10:06,120
He's even a one-eyed
Samurai, just like Riyuma.

132
00:10:44,260 --> 00:10:46,620
Looks like this is the end of the road.

133
00:10:46,980 --> 00:10:50,757
You can't see the moon, so your
Sulong form won't save you.

134
00:10:50,840 --> 00:10:54,180
Good night, King of the Day!

135
00:10:58,800 --> 00:11:04,760
I forgive you by lying about
the samurai you're hiding.

136
00:11:05,360 --> 00:11:08,440
You already paid the
price with your country.

137
00:11:16,480 --> 00:11:19,777
This is your last chance
to bring rice home.

138
00:11:19,860 --> 00:11:22,220
Otherwise, your leg is coming off.

139
00:11:22,400 --> 00:11:25,040
I swear that I don't
know anyone named Race.

140
00:11:25,400 --> 00:11:27,700
If he's here, I'll cut my own belly.

141
00:11:29,280 --> 00:11:30,560
You are born.

142
00:11:31,340 --> 00:11:32,620
Now suffer!

143
00:11:39,800 --> 00:11:44,200
We would have laid down our lives
a hundred times to protect Race.

144
00:11:44,560 --> 00:11:46,320
Our honor demanded it.

145
00:11:49,860 --> 00:11:53,260
I would have been too ashamed
to return if I had failed.

146
00:11:53,820 --> 00:11:55,420
Are those your last words?

147
00:11:55,720 --> 00:11:58,420
Cause I'm cutting off your head this time!

148
00:12:02,860 --> 00:12:07,820
We have been preparing for this battle
ever since the day Lord Odin died!

149
00:12:10,980 --> 00:12:14,500
We'll avenge our fallen
lord and save Wano!

150
00:12:28,420 --> 00:12:32,697
For two decades we've
asked ourselves are we

151
00:12:32,780 --> 00:12:36,817
still lord odin samurai
here is the answer?

152
00:12:36,900 --> 00:12:42,417
Enough what no how did

153
00:12:42,500 --> 00:12:44,040
you transform again?

154
00:12:45,580 --> 00:12:48,860
Damn it there's a hole in the ceiling

155
00:12:55,860 --> 00:13:01,260
You'll never defile the name
of Kozuki Odin ever again!

156
00:13:18,860 --> 00:13:22,460
We had to reach the final
battle, no matter the cost.

157
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:30,840
If an ancient city must fall
for us to win, so be it.

158
00:13:34,340 --> 00:13:38,060
If we must sacrifice our lives
to win, then we are ready.

159
00:13:47,040 --> 00:13:50,220
Our victory will bring
a new dawn to the world.

160
00:13:59,560 --> 00:14:02,501
These enemies just keep
pouring out of the castle!

161
00:14:15,860 --> 00:14:16,690
Stay back.

162
00:14:16,960 --> 00:14:20,254
The battle taking place here
is far beyond men like you.

163
00:14:20,720 --> 00:14:21,900
Screw you, pal.

164
00:14:22,160 --> 00:14:23,077
This is our base.

165
00:14:23,160 --> 00:14:23,990
You can't stop us.

166
00:14:24,073 --> 00:14:26,057
You get out of our way or you die.

167
00:14:26,140 --> 00:14:26,970
What'll it be?

168
00:14:27,060 --> 00:14:31,200
If you boys want to stay
alive, I suggest you leave.

169
00:14:34,780 --> 00:14:35,610
Coroneago.

170
00:14:38,220 --> 00:14:39,560
Hello there, Carrot.

171
00:14:39,740 --> 00:14:42,820
Hello there, Wanda. It's Mr. Catviper.

172
00:14:43,140 --> 00:14:47,060
I appreciate you, Karoo, leaving
a piece of this bastard for me.

173
00:14:47,840 --> 00:14:49,120
Let's end this.

174
00:14:51,160 --> 00:14:55,631
If it weren't for Pedro, Luffy and his
allies never would have made it here.

175
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:59,824
This raid would have failed before
it even had a chance to start.

176
00:15:00,080 --> 00:15:00,910
Pedro again?

177
00:15:00,993 --> 00:15:03,877
You really, Lickety, loved
that bastard, didn't you?

178
00:15:03,960 --> 00:15:10,680
Thinking back on my old friend, I can't
help but gaze at that beautiful full moon.

179
00:15:14,660 --> 00:15:17,320
I'll give Yugara a show, Pedro.

180
00:15:17,820 --> 00:15:19,600
Have a drink or two and enjoy.

181
00:15:25,960 --> 00:15:29,280
Look to the sky, you slobbering Knight.

182
00:15:32,660 --> 00:15:38,200
The view of tonight's full
moon shall be your last.

183
00:15:45,920 --> 00:15:48,837
I thought you were a fool
for serving the ghost

184
00:15:48,920 --> 00:15:51,117
but on second thought
serving that breath is even.

185
00:15:51,200 --> 00:15:53,080
Ah! Silence!

186
00:15:53,440 --> 00:15:55,028
Use is nothing to laugh at!

187
00:15:55,180 --> 00:16:00,380
I was a scoundrel who grew up to be a
samurai, so our lord can grow as well!

188
00:16:00,640 --> 00:16:04,120
Mono will watch over him, as
he will watch over us someday!

189
00:16:04,660 --> 00:16:07,120
But you will not look to see that!

190
00:16:07,820 --> 00:16:09,460
Shadow-pone-jutsu!

191
00:16:14,100 --> 00:16:19,820
With the strength and dedication of
my ninpo, I shall defeat my enemies!

192
00:16:24,600 --> 00:16:25,940
Whoa, you're kidding!

193
00:16:32,700 --> 00:16:33,940
What the hell?

194
00:16:34,220 --> 00:16:35,980
Is that thing a giant dragon?

195
00:16:37,880 --> 00:16:39,220
Why is he here?

196
00:16:39,520 --> 00:16:41,240
Who invited a dragon?

197
00:16:41,940 --> 00:16:44,120
That must be Kaido. What do we do?

198
00:16:44,840 --> 00:16:45,757
Should we fight?

199
00:16:45,840 --> 00:16:46,860
I'm not so sure.

200
00:16:47,080 --> 00:16:49,020
You can count me out. No way!

201
00:16:55,980 --> 00:16:58,980
You will never make a snack out of me!

202
00:16:59,220 --> 00:17:01,660
If you try, I will swallow you whole!

203
00:17:02,080 --> 00:17:03,120
Please step away!

204
00:17:06,740 --> 00:17:08,680
Straw Hat! Be careful!

205
00:17:09,060 --> 00:17:10,354
You sure you're ready?

206
00:17:22,660 --> 00:17:23,740
Are you, Momo?

207
00:17:24,660 --> 00:17:25,490
Indeed.

208
00:17:26,040 --> 00:17:26,880
The kid?

209
00:17:27,040 --> 00:17:28,275
What happened to him?

210
00:17:28,620 --> 00:17:30,760
So, Kaido, is it here? What?

211
00:17:31,560 --> 00:17:34,680
I used my right pride
jutsu on Lord Momonosuke.

212
00:17:34,920 --> 00:17:37,157
I didn't want to do it, but he begged me.

213
00:17:37,240 --> 00:17:40,360
So I turned him into a
28-year-old at his request.

214
00:17:40,700 --> 00:17:42,465
Your power can really do that?

215
00:17:44,700 --> 00:17:45,920
Why are you crying?

216
00:17:47,560 --> 00:17:48,600
Oh, because...

217
00:17:52,640 --> 00:17:54,260
My lord, you!

218
00:17:54,420 --> 00:17:56,720
You look just like you!

219
00:18:10,080 --> 00:18:10,910
Alright!

220
00:18:10,993 --> 00:18:12,580
Let's go, Momo!

221
00:18:12,940 --> 00:18:14,480
We're taking back Wano!

222
00:18:14,800 --> 00:18:15,737
Are you ready?

223
00:18:15,820 --> 00:18:16,960
Of course!

224
00:18:18,680 --> 00:18:19,510
Ah!

225
00:18:32,740 --> 00:18:33,570
What?

226
00:18:33,840 --> 00:18:35,540
Crock, Krieg.

227
00:18:36,720 --> 00:18:37,980
What's going on?

228
00:18:38,100 --> 00:18:39,394
Why did they collapse?

229
00:18:39,640 --> 00:18:41,540
Did something happen, you guys?

230
00:18:41,780 --> 00:18:43,240
Come on, get up!

231
00:18:44,480 --> 00:18:45,897
Oh, it can't be!

232
00:18:45,980 --> 00:18:48,720
This guy can use Kakarazaki!

233
00:18:52,860 --> 00:18:54,760
Seems you figured it out.

234
00:18:55,080 --> 00:18:56,700
Krieg, that's not good!

235
00:18:57,860 --> 00:19:00,337
This is the fate of all who dare to bask

236
00:19:00,420 --> 00:19:03,008
in my presence before
stealing their hearts.

237
00:19:03,860 --> 00:19:06,960
I did take down two Tobiropo after all.

238
00:19:07,360 --> 00:19:10,477
Why, you might as well call
me Sibling Hunter Usohachi!

239
00:19:10,560 --> 00:19:11,980
The Tobiropo!

240
00:19:12,440 --> 00:19:13,640
Two of them!

241
00:19:17,880 --> 00:19:19,700
You can't defy my strength.

242
00:19:19,960 --> 00:19:21,620
Join me by my side.

243
00:19:30,600 --> 00:19:34,835
I don't know why all the bad guys are
passing out, but it sure is handy.

244
00:19:35,280 --> 00:19:38,633
It's because Big Mom is fighting
on the same floor as us.

245
00:19:39,040 --> 00:19:43,393
Only the strong are able to withstand
the power of her conqueror's Haki.

246
00:19:45,140 --> 00:19:47,740
Franky, do you know
what happened to Luffy?

247
00:19:48,020 --> 00:19:49,577
I don't know anything you don't know.

248
00:19:49,660 --> 00:19:52,557
I think what Momo said earlier
is all that matters, though!

249
00:19:52,640 --> 00:19:54,880
Luffy is still alive!

250
00:19:55,320 --> 00:19:57,140
I can hear his voice now!

251
00:19:57,820 --> 00:20:00,173
And he promised me that he'll come back!

252
00:20:00,600 --> 00:20:02,297
I wonder where Momo is?

253
00:20:02,380 --> 00:20:05,380
Shinobu was with him, but
I can't reach her either.

254
00:20:07,140 --> 00:20:09,957
You know what they say,
no news is good news!

255
00:20:10,040 --> 00:20:11,957
Come on, you are not helping.

256
00:20:12,040 --> 00:20:14,746
When you finish your
job, hustle on down here.

257
00:20:17,300 --> 00:20:21,300
Enemy troops are pouring into the
performance floor all of a sudden.

258
00:20:21,980 --> 00:20:23,900
You sure could use a hand. What?

259
00:20:24,040 --> 00:20:25,334
The performance floor?

260
00:20:26,400 --> 00:20:28,120
Hold your ground, bros.

261
00:20:28,280 --> 00:20:30,480
We can't let a single one of them in.

262
00:20:30,980 --> 00:20:33,977
Zoro and Sanshi are fighting two
of the lead performers in there,

263
00:20:34,060 --> 00:20:35,825
and they can't afford to lose.

264
00:20:37,280 --> 00:20:40,097
Aye, aye, but that doesn't
mean I take orders from you.

265
00:20:40,180 --> 00:20:42,640
We're eight boxes! Don't forget it!

266
00:20:46,900 --> 00:20:48,320
Ow! Fire!

267
00:20:48,660 --> 00:20:50,013
Please stop burning me!

268
00:20:50,360 --> 00:20:53,180
Although it would make
sense to cremate me!

269
00:20:54,220 --> 00:20:56,840
No, I'm not ready for that yet!

270
00:20:59,540 --> 00:21:01,840
I still have best to protect!

271
00:21:02,660 --> 00:21:04,720
It's Ferran Corpse! What happened?

272
00:21:05,900 --> 00:21:08,537
The short of it is we need to
get out of the castle quickly.

273
00:21:08,620 --> 00:21:11,637
Do any of you minks know
how the raid is progressing?

274
00:21:11,720 --> 00:21:13,661
All I've seen out there is chaos.

275
00:21:14,040 --> 00:21:18,277
That reminds me, on the way here, I
ran into Jinbei on the fourth floor.

276
00:21:18,360 --> 00:21:19,280
I'm a ball!

277
00:21:36,820 --> 00:21:38,920
Heribus Brickfield!

278
00:21:48,540 --> 00:21:50,658
I haven't heard any news in a while.

279
00:21:50,880 --> 00:21:53,957
Is your captain still battling
against Kaido on the roof?

280
00:21:54,040 --> 00:21:54,920
He beats me.

281
00:21:55,320 --> 00:21:57,497
I've been too busy fighting to find out.

282
00:21:57,580 --> 00:21:58,410
I see.

283
00:21:58,860 --> 00:22:00,919
We can't get bogged down like this.

284
00:22:01,080 --> 00:22:04,786
We need to find the strong
opponents and focus on them instead.

285
00:22:07,400 --> 00:22:09,260
Jimmy, help! It's me, Brook.

286
00:22:09,500 --> 00:22:10,937
We have a situation here.

287
00:22:11,020 --> 00:22:13,997
There's a fire down here on the
third floor, and it's spreading fast.

288
00:22:14,080 --> 00:22:16,537
If you want to get downstairs,
then you'd better hurry!

289
00:22:16,620 --> 00:22:17,450
A fire?

290
00:22:17,533 --> 00:22:20,077
That doesn't sound good, but wait,

291
00:22:20,160 --> 00:22:24,340
the roof, who's keeping
Kaido busy up there?

292
00:22:50,980 --> 00:22:55,197
Give it up, you're
never gonna become Odin.

293
00:22:55,280 --> 00:23:00,457
Why should I listen to
the man who wants me dead?

294
00:23:00,540 --> 00:23:02,217
That was your doing.

295
00:23:02,300 --> 00:23:06,997
This isn't a family quarrel
and it isn't a game.

296
00:23:07,080 --> 00:23:11,797
If you take the name of Odin,
you must be prepared for war.

297
00:23:11,880 --> 00:23:13,520
Do you understand?

298
00:23:17,580 --> 00:23:21,500
You think I should be
punished for admiring someone?

299
00:23:27,040 --> 00:23:31,180
I love Odin, but you can't
take that away from me!

300
00:23:43,160 --> 00:23:46,760
BALLS, I 'LL PROTECT THE
LAND OF WADO, OUT OF MY WAY!

301
00:23:48,700 --> 00:23:51,880
NOW ALL THEN THE PORTERS OF WADO ARE Tang!

302
00:23:52,140 --> 00:23:53,900
Was she always this violent?

303
00:23:54,180 --> 00:23:57,057
No, but she's been terrorizing
us like this all week!

304
00:23:57,140 --> 00:23:58,022
Keep your cool!

305
00:23:58,160 --> 00:23:58,990
Huh?

306
00:23:59,073 --> 00:24:01,848
She may be Commander Kaido's
daughter, but she's still a kid.

307
00:24:01,960 --> 00:24:04,497
There's no way she can
take us all on at once.

308
00:24:04,580 --> 00:24:05,933
Charge in and stop her!

309
00:24:06,080 --> 00:24:07,640
You think you can stop me?

310
00:24:07,860 --> 00:24:09,180
Just try it!

311
00:24:09,340 --> 00:24:10,560
I'll never lose!

312
00:24:21,640 --> 00:24:23,740
I'm begging you, just come quietly!

313
00:24:24,380 --> 00:24:25,460
Please, princess!

314
00:24:25,980 --> 00:24:27,000
I said no! No!

315
00:24:27,120 --> 00:24:28,238
I'm not a princess!

316
00:24:29,580 --> 00:24:30,897
I am...

317
00:24:30,980 --> 00:24:32,080
RUNNING!

318
00:24:39,300 --> 00:24:41,740
She didn't even touch him, did she?

319
00:24:58,700 --> 00:25:03,380
Are you the one responsible
for all this? Yamato? Shut up!

320
00:25:03,600 --> 00:25:06,040
I'm Odin, not Yamato!

321
00:25:10,700 --> 00:25:11,900
I'm Odin!

322
00:25:12,120 --> 00:25:13,708
Answer my question, Yamato.

323
00:25:14,080 --> 00:25:16,374
Are you the one who did this to my men?

324
00:25:16,740 --> 00:25:17,680
I don't know.

325
00:25:18,140 --> 00:25:20,081
They just collapsed on their own.

326
00:25:21,920 --> 00:25:22,750
Hey!

327
00:25:22,833 --> 00:25:24,517
Get these chains off of me, father!

328
00:25:24,600 --> 00:25:28,140
If you don't feed me, I'm gonna die!

329
00:25:28,640 --> 00:25:30,540
Conqueror's Haki, interesting.

330
00:25:31,520 --> 00:25:33,200
You have potential.

331
00:25:33,860 --> 00:25:37,820
But if you've decided you
want to be Odin, then die.

332
00:25:38,180 --> 00:25:39,020
We're enemies!

333
00:25:40,080 --> 00:25:41,040
Hey, stop!

334
00:25:44,560 --> 00:25:47,442
Why don't you cool your
head in here for a while?

335
00:25:47,660 --> 00:25:49,580
A month ought to do the trick.

336
00:25:54,600 --> 00:25:55,717
Where are you going?

337
00:25:55,800 --> 00:25:58,020
Don't leave me in here! It's dark!

338
00:25:59,120 --> 00:26:00,640
A whole month, Commander?

339
00:26:01,120 --> 00:26:05,120
The Ogre Princess is tough, but
there's no way she can survive that!

340
00:26:05,560 --> 00:26:09,057
Besides, there are samurai from the
land of Wano locked up in there!

341
00:26:09,140 --> 00:26:11,140
They're as dangerous as they come!

342
00:26:11,440 --> 00:26:14,420
I'll grant you the same
mercy as my idiot child.

343
00:26:15,020 --> 00:26:18,000
You have one month to get in line.

344
00:26:19,560 --> 00:26:23,097
If you change your mind, shout
through the air hole in the ceiling.

345
00:26:23,180 --> 00:26:25,239
Tell them you want to join my army.

346
00:26:25,360 --> 00:26:27,478
Then I'll let you out of this place.

347
00:26:28,320 --> 00:26:31,261
How many days has it been
since you ate something?

348
00:26:32,300 --> 00:26:33,720
Here, go ahead.

349
00:26:34,240 --> 00:26:35,420
You can have dinner.

350
00:26:36,240 --> 00:26:37,900
Or one of you can.

351
00:26:41,660 --> 00:26:44,307
Swordsmen should not be
without their swords.

352
00:26:45,180 --> 00:26:46,010
Father!

353
00:26:48,360 --> 00:26:50,057
That's not what I know, you're my dad!

354
00:26:50,140 --> 00:26:51,320
They're angry!

355
00:26:51,540 --> 00:26:52,700
It's not safe!

356
00:26:53,000 --> 00:26:54,837
You can't give them their swords!

357
00:26:54,920 --> 00:26:56,214
They're gonna kill me!

358
00:26:56,740 --> 00:26:58,920
Now, why would they want to kill you?

359
00:26:59,260 --> 00:27:01,460
I thought you said you were Odin.

360
00:27:12,920 --> 00:27:17,640
Although I'm Odin, I'm also the
son of Kaido, who killed Odin.

361
00:27:21,140 --> 00:27:24,728
It would be too easy for those
samurai to take their revenge.

362
00:27:26,060 --> 00:27:29,472
Father only put that food there
so we would fight over it.

363
00:27:29,660 --> 00:27:31,660
He wants us to kill each other.

364
00:27:40,500 --> 00:27:43,117
But there's no point in
me thinking about that.

365
00:27:43,200 --> 00:27:45,024
They're going to kill me first.

366
00:27:54,660 --> 00:27:55,660
Go on.

367
00:27:57,020 --> 00:27:57,850
What?

368
00:27:58,200 --> 00:27:59,340
Help yourself.

369
00:28:01,740 --> 00:28:02,720
Don't worry.

370
00:28:02,940 --> 00:28:04,528
Some of I don't get hungry.

371
00:28:05,720 --> 00:28:06,550
Really?

372
00:28:08,360 --> 00:28:11,660
I mean, are you sure about this?

373
00:28:12,120 --> 00:28:13,540
Because I'll eat it.

374
00:28:13,800 --> 00:28:17,177
I'm really hungry, so I'll eat the
whole thing if you don't want it.

375
00:28:17,260 --> 00:28:18,090
Can I?

376
00:28:19,000 --> 00:28:20,220
Of course you can.

377
00:28:20,620 --> 00:28:22,738
Your father's sins are not your own.

378
00:28:24,520 --> 00:28:25,760
I am grateful.

379
00:28:29,380 --> 00:28:31,240
Your jam and I are so tough.

380
00:28:31,360 --> 00:28:33,536
I can't believe you don't get hungry.

381
00:29:13,760 --> 00:29:17,380
Hey, can I become a samurai,
even though I get hungry?

382
00:29:25,040 --> 00:29:26,180
Hands in the air.

383
00:29:26,580 --> 00:29:27,520
Yes, sir!

384
00:29:39,120 --> 00:29:40,180
Calm yourself.

385
00:29:40,760 --> 00:29:43,220
You said that you're Kozuki Odin, right?

386
00:29:43,580 --> 00:29:46,577
We overheard your talk, and I understand.

387
00:29:46,660 --> 00:29:48,720
We love Odin as much as you do.

388
00:29:53,580 --> 00:29:56,180
What name does a fallen Samurai need?

389
00:29:58,900 --> 00:30:01,000
Just call me so-and-so.

390
00:30:04,940 --> 00:30:10,017
I found too many hard words you

391
00:30:10,100 --> 00:30:11,997
had Odin's travel log all this time,

392
00:30:12,080 --> 00:30:12,910
but how?

393
00:30:14,960 --> 00:30:19,977
This world has four seas as well
as one long and narrow waterway.

394
00:30:20,060 --> 00:30:23,717
Apparently he says the planet's
round just like a dumpling.

395
00:30:23,800 --> 00:30:25,797
What a mysterious thing.

396
00:30:25,880 --> 00:30:30,997
How long has it been?

397
00:30:31,080 --> 00:30:31,957
10 days.

398
00:30:32,040 --> 00:30:33,917
I already lost count.

399
00:30:34,000 --> 00:30:35,837
It's all starting to blur together.

400
00:30:35,920 --> 00:30:38,097
Kaido is too cruel.

401
00:30:38,180 --> 00:30:40,977
I can't believe he would let
his own child die like this.

402
00:30:41,060 --> 00:30:42,417
At this rate,

403
00:30:42,500 --> 00:30:46,477
I fear we may not live long enough to
see the battle that Odin predicted.

404
00:30:46,560 --> 00:30:50,917
It'll happen, and when it does,

405
00:30:51,000 --> 00:30:54,397
I'll fight on the side
of Wano and its people.

406
00:30:54,480 --> 00:30:58,037
I'll go out to see like Odin.

407
00:30:58,120 --> 00:31:00,737
I'll become stronger and stronger.

408
00:31:00,820 --> 00:31:04,440
In that case, I won't worry.

409
00:31:05,160 --> 00:31:06,597
Our path is clear.

410
00:31:06,680 --> 00:31:10,657
Dead or alive, there's an important
role for us to play in that war.

411
00:31:10,740 --> 00:31:13,660
To ensure that you won't die here.

412
00:31:18,140 --> 00:31:20,257
20 years is a long time.

413
00:31:20,340 --> 00:31:23,200
Too long for us to wait. I'm afraid.

414
00:31:26,340 --> 00:31:27,811
Wives, you can't do that!

415
00:31:28,060 --> 00:31:30,413
My father is going to kill you for sure!

416
00:31:30,960 --> 00:31:34,677
I'm not going to stay here and
spend my final days rotting away.

417
00:31:34,760 --> 00:31:36,936
We never intended to give in to Kaido

418
00:31:37,780 --> 00:31:39,020
This is the end.

419
00:31:47,860 --> 00:31:50,600
We'll leave the land of Wano to you!

420
00:32:05,300 --> 00:32:09,380
I'm not afraid of you, because
there are people who believe in me,

421
00:32:09,600 --> 00:32:11,880
who accept me for who I am!

422
00:32:14,900 --> 00:32:18,297
Why do you want to take away the
freedom of one of those people?

423
00:32:18,380 --> 00:32:19,840
To take away my freedom?

424
00:32:20,340 --> 00:32:25,620
Life is more than just a series of
questions and answers, you ignorant brats!

425
00:32:32,260 --> 00:32:33,660
WONDERPOWER!
